  partName: ExhaustManifoldBolt
  description: The ExhaustManifoldBolt is a tiny, elongated fastener positioned at
    the top-center-rear of the engine, responsible for securing the exhaust manifold
    in place. Made of Frame material, this bolt is designed to withstand the high
    temperatures and stresses generated by the exhaust system. Interestingly, the
    ExhaustManifoldBolt's location allows it to be easily accessed for maintenance
    and repairs.
